SEE ALSO
     stty(1), execve(2), exec(3), tty(4)

BUGS
     Strictly speaking, since _i_o_c_t_l may be extended in different
     ways to devices with different properties, _a_r_g_p should have
     an open-ended declaration like

          union { struct sgttyb ...; ...  } *argp;

     The important thing is that the size is fixed by `struct
     sgttyb'.

ASSEMBLER
     (ioctl = 54.)
     sys ioctl; fildes; request; argp

     (stty = 31.)
     (file descriptor in r0)
     stty; argp

     (gtty = 32.)
     (file descriptor in r0)
     sys gtty; argp

